From b2548287a869fd16e159076b990e4b881e7546d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 20:49:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Vendor HAWK reference C as pqm4 m4 baseline

Replace the earlier scaffold with the full HAWK reference implementation
from hawk-sign/dev (MIT, (c) 2022 Hawk Project, Pornin & Pulles),
vendored into crypto_sign/hawk512/m4 with the NIST API adapted to pqm4
conventions (size_t length types, pqm4's randombytes hooked through a
hawk_rng shim). HAWK keygen pulls in the embedded NTRUgen sampler/solver
(ng_*.c) so no separate ntrugen integration is required at the C level.

crypto_sign/hawk1024/m4 follows the upstream ml-dsa-44/65/87 pattern:
api.h and api.c hold the per-variant constants (LOGN=10, 360/2440/1221),
while every shared core source is symlinked to ../../hawk512/m4.

This commit is the baseline that compiles and runs end-to-end; the
optimization roadmap (Plantard NTT port for Q=18433, SHAKE-256 swap to
pqm4 assembly, NTRUgen recursive-base-case M4 asm, isochronous CDT
sampler) is recorded in crypto_sign/hawk512/m4/NOTES.md and the
implementation will land in subsequent commits.
